# spelled.z -- a program whose own unit `os` (os.z beside it, with its own C
# implementation file os/nativec.zd) is spelled like the standard library's. A
# unit is the standard library's by its file, not its spelling, so both natives
# run this program's rows: cpuCount, a key the served os has too, prints this
# unit's 4242 and not the machine's count; conjure, a key only this unit has,
# is found at all.

main: function is {
    print "\{os.cpuCount}"
    print "\{os.conjure n: 7.i64}"
}
